<https://cnw-ld.org/work/SchWB2-430>
    a frbr:Work, mo:MusicalWork ;
    dcterms:title "Musica per l'eseqvie di Louisa regina di Danemarca"@it ;
    dcterms:identifier "SchW B2:430" ;
    cnw:cnwNumber "B2:430" ;
    cnw:catalogueCode "SchW" ;
    dcterms:creator <https://cnw-ld.org/agent/johann_adolph_scheibe> ;
    cnw:textAuthor <https://cnw-ld.org/agent/gerhard_schaft> ;
    dcterms:created "January 1752" ;
    dcterms:language "Danish" ;
    dcterms:language "English" ;
    dcterms:language "Italian" ;
    dcterms:subject "Vocal music" ;
    dcterms:subject "Cantata" ;
    dcterms:subject "Music for vocal soloists and instruments with or without choir" ;
    dcterms:subject "Occasional" ;
    dcterms:subject "Secular" ;
    cnw:editorialNote "'Saa snart Hans Majestet Allerhøyst Selv derpaa indfinder sig i Kirken, begynder Guds-Tienesten med en Sørge-Musiqve, som varer i det Længste 20 Minuter, hvornæst Biskop Hersleb holder en Dansk Prædiken over Esaiæ 38 Cap. 17 v. som varer i det høyeste en Time, derpaa en Sørge-Musiqve af 20 Minuter, hvorefter den første Hof-Prædikant Bluhme, holder den anden Prædiken i det Tydske Sprog over forbemeldte Text og besluttes endeligen Guds-Tienesten med en Sørge-Musiqve af 20 Minuter eller fleere Minuter. Medens den sidste Sørge-Musiqve vedvarer, tilbagebringes, som før er meldt, Hendes Majestæts Crone paa sædvanlig Maade udi det Kongelige inderste Forgemak [...]'" ;
    cnw:editorialNote "The review mentions that at the previous concert a German 'Trauer-Cantate' was performed by a learned author (no name is mentioned and neither is the composer). The event was most likely 3 February 1751. One of the text sources is in fact bound with a libretto 'Trauer-Kantate, bey Gelegenheit des am 19 Decemb. 1751. [...] den 3ten Februar, 1752.' (DK-Kk, E 7292 4o); see SchW B7:001." ;
    cnw:editorialNote "Scheibe mentions the work in connection with a performance of it in The Musical Society." ;
    cnw:editorialNote "In margin at stave Scheibe has written 'Tenore'; however, he employs the C1-clef indicating a cantus part. The part might have been ascribed to either 'Dyden' or 'Kiærlighed'." ;
    frbr:realization <https://cnw-ld.org/work/SchWB2-430/expression/1> ;
    cnw:performanceCount 1 .

